{{also|Blud|блуд}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/blʌd/}}
{{rfap|en}}

===Etymology 1===
Created in [[Multicultural London English]], of [[Jamaican]] origin. Has since spread around [[England]], and thence [[Anglosphere]] and online. Claimed to be, via [[eye dialect]] spelling, from Caribbean Creole {{m|en|blood||family relation, close friend}} (compare {{m|en|blood brother}}). Possibly derived or reinforced from {{m|en|brother}}; compare {{m|en|bro}}, {{m|en|bruh}}, {{m|en|brudder}} etc. 

